@startuml Collaboration to History — Session End & Cleanup
!theme plain
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Collaboration -> History Service — Session End & Cleanup

actor "User A" as UA
actor "User B" as UB
participant "Frontend A" as FEA
participant "Frontend B" as FEB
participant "Collab Service\n(Socket.IO)" as Collab
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "History Service" as HS
database "Redis\n(Sessions)" as Redis
database "Firestore\n(session_history)" as FS

== Active Session ==

UA <-> Collab: /editor — Yjs updates (WebSocket)
UB <-> Collab: /editor — Yjs updates (WebSocket)
UA <-> Collab: /chat — messages (WebSocket)
UB <-> Collab: /chat — messages (WebSocket)

note over Collab, Redis
  During the session, every code edit triggers:
  - RPUSH session:{id}:ydoc (Yjs binary update, base64)
  - SET session:{id}:finalCode (plaintext snapshot)
  Chat messages stored via RPUSH session:{id}:chat
  (trimmed to last 500 with LTRIM)
end note

== User A Ends Session (explicit) ==

UA -> FEA: Click "End Session"
FEA -> Collab: emit 'end-session' (/editor)
activate Collab
Collab -> Collab: Snapshot code:\nydoc.getText('code').toString()

Collab -> GW: POST /internal/collab/user-ended/{sessionId}\n{userId: A, finalCode: "<snapshot>"}
activate GW
GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:meta
Redis --> GW: {user1_id, user2_id, questionId, ...}
GW -> GW: Build history payload\n{...meta, sessionId, finalCode,\nendedAt, submittedBy: A}
GW -> HS: POST /history
activate HS
HS -> FS: Set document({sessionId}_{uid_A})\nin session_history collection
FS --> HS: OK
HS --> GW: 201 Created
deactivate HS
GW -> Redis: DELETE active_session:{uid_A}
GW -> Redis: SET session:{id}:saved:{uid_A} "1" EX 7200
GW --> Collab: 200 {detail: "History saved for A"}
deactivate GW

Collab -> UB: emit 'partner-ended'\n{userId: A}
deactivate Collab

FEA -> GW: POST /collab/end-session/{sessionId}\nAuth: [JWT_A]
activate GW
GW -> Redis: DELETE active_session:{uid_A}
note right: Idempotent — may already\nbe cleared by internal endpoint
GW --> FEA: 200 {detail: "Active session cleared"}
deactivate GW
FEA -> FEA: navigate('/dashboard')

note over UB, FEB: User B sees modal:\n"Partner left. Continue or End?"

== User B Chooses "Continue Coding" ==

UB -> FEB: Dismiss modal,\ncontinue editing solo

note over UB, Collab: User B can keep editing.\nCode changes still persist to Redis.

== User B Eventually Ends Session ==

UB -> FEB: Click "End Session"
FEB -> Collab: emit 'end-session' (/editor)
activate Collab
Collab -> Collab: Snapshot updated code

Collab -> GW: POST /internal/collab/user-ended/{sessionId}\n{userId: B, finalCode: "<updated snapshot>"}
activate GW
GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:meta
GW -> GW: Build history payload\n{...meta, finalCode, endedAt, submittedBy: B}
GW -> HS: POST /history
activate HS
HS -> FS: Set document({sessionId}_{uid_B})\nin session_history collection
FS --> HS: OK
HS --> GW: 201 Created
deactivate HS
GW -> Redis: DELETE active_session:{uid_B}
GW -> Redis: SET session:{id}:saved:{uid_B} "1" EX 7200
GW --> Collab: 200
deactivate GW
deactivate Collab

FEB -> GW: POST /collab/end-session/{sessionId}\nAuth: [JWT_B]
GW -> Redis: DELETE active_session:{uid_B}
GW --> FEB: 200

UB ->x Collab: /editor WebSocket disconnect

== Alternative: User Disconnects Without Ending ==

note over Collab
  If a user disconnects without emitting 'end-session'
  (e.g., closes browser tab, network failure):
end note

UA ->x Collab: /editor WebSocket disconnect
activate Collab
Collab -> Collab: Remove userId from\nconnectedEditors set
Collab -> UB: emit 'user-left'\n{userId: A, message: "Partner disconnected"}

Collab -> Collab: Start **30s per-user timer**\nfor User A

alt User A reconnects within 30s
    UA -> Collab: Reconnect /editor\n(new ticket required)
    Collab -> Collab: Clear User A's timer\nRe-add to connectedEditors
    Collab -> UB: emit 'user-joined' {userId: A}
else 30s timer expires — treat as end-session
    Collab -> Collab: Snapshot code
    Collab -> GW: POST /internal/collab/user-ended/{sessionId}\n{userId: A, finalCode}
    GW -> HS: POST /history (save A's history)
    GW -> Redis: DELETE active_session:{uid_A}
    GW -> Redis: SET session:{id}:saved:{uid_A} "1" EX 7200
    GW --> Collab: 200
    Collab -> UB: emit 'partner-ended' {userId: A}
end
deactivate Collab

== All Users Gone — Final Cleanup (5s timer) ==

note over Collab
  When the last user's 30s disconnect timer expires
  and connectedEditors.size == 0, a **5s session
  cleanup timer** starts.
end note

Collab -> Collab: connectedEditors.size == 0\nStart **5s cleanup timer**

activate Collab
Collab -> GW: POST /internal/collab/session-ended/{sessionId}
activate GW

GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:meta
GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:saved:{uid_A}
GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:saved:{uid_B}

alt User not yet saved
    GW -> GW: Build history from meta + finalCode
    GW -> HS: POST /history (fallback save)
end

note over GW: Check saved flags for each user.\nSkip if already saved via end-session\nor disconnect timeout.

GW -> Redis: DELETE session:{id}:meta\nsession:{id}:finalCode\nsession:{id}:ydoc\nsession:{id}:chat\nsession:{id}:saved:{uid_A}\nsession:{id}:saved:{uid_B}\nactive_session:{uid_A}\nactive_session:{uid_B}
Redis --> GW: OK

GW --> Collab: 200 {detail: "Session ended\nand history saved"}
deactivate GW

Collab -> Collab: sessions.delete(sessionId)\n(remove from in-memory Map)
deactivate Collab

@enduml
